# Absolute path to the data directory on the HOST machine.
#
# The backend runs inside Docker and spawns child containers via the Docker socket.
# Volume mounts in those child containers use HOST-side paths (as seen by the Docker
# daemon), so this must be an absolute path on your host filesystem.
#
# Example (Linux/macOS):
#   HOST_DATA_DIR=/home/alice/diagnostic-servers-webapp/data
#
# 'make start' sets this automatically to $(pwd)/data.
HOST_DATA_DIR=
